    text: "Current full npm coverage run has reported two existing acceptance problems outside the round-4 changes: bounded final failure under the owned-child cleanup retry test in test/controller-boundaries.test.ts, whose settlement guard is 8000 ms; and SIGKILL at every HTTP-to-PM receipt boundary in test/decision-recovery.test.ts, cancelled at its unchanged 300000 ms limit. These are observations, not yet classified as host-only flakes. The rest of the suite continues so complete counts and final failure details are retained. Focused isolated retries will follow before any final validation claim; no source or timeout changes were made for these cases."
