    text: "Coverage fix and quick-tier timing work. Coverage: added a deterministic LM Compose controller drill in test/lm-compose.test.ts that runs the real durable loop with the compose-lm adapter; only the container runtime is a PATH-injected stand-in whose compose run executes the packaged process-lm-trainer.ts entrypoint, so no Docker daemon is needed. It reaches the external process trainer fit path (index.ts 4557-4558 plus its durable verify call) and exercises verifyLmProcessJob success, missing-receipt and digest-drift refusals (process-lm.ts 60-64) at every depth. Thresholds and ignores unchanged. Sampling: new testKindCases helper in test/support/depth.ts keeps one representative of every declared kind at quick depth and stays exhaustive at full depth, with contract tests in test/depth.test.ts. Applied to the remaining full enumerations: durable-snapshot corruption receipt sweep (legacy, first and latest cycle receipts at quick), HTTP-to-PM receipt SIGKILL stages (every crash stage kind and both decision metrics without all 8 combinations), refused-vector boundary crashes (phase crash kind once; the durable-loop phase sweep already covers collect/train/evaluate crash points at quick), and the generated SDK chronology inversions (one inversion per artifact-class pair per shape). Job shape: Node 22 quick tests now run in a non-required quick-shard (22, 1/2) matrix via node --test --test-shard, and the required test (22) check is an always() aggregate that needs the shards and fails unless every shard succeeded; docs/tracker PRs keep the same health, changelog, audit, pack and docs-input contracts in the aggregate. test (26) is unchanged. Local verification on the shared host: typecheck, test typecheck, lint, duplicates, docstring, changelog check and identity audit passed; touched tests passed at quick depth: depth contracts 4/4, LM Compose controller drill (new), HTTP receipt replay, refused vector retries 6/6, chronology witnesses, immutable snapshot corruption property; workflow and release contract tests 36/36. Hosted CI timing and coverage results are pending from the pushed run."
  - created_at: "2026-11-16T03:49:09.631Z"
    author: pi-glm
    text: "Pushed head 9c4a511 (worktree branch ci/quick-pr-tier-deep-local-tier, ahead of the prior unpushed receipt commit 6a9e94f which is included). CI run 43800153216 started at 03:46:33Z with quick-shard (22, 1), quick-shard (22, 2) and test (26) running; the required test (22) aggregate waits on the shards. Hosted per-job and per-step wall times will be recorded from the jobs API after completion; observation is bounded to 30 minutes after this last push."
  - created_at: "2026-11-16T04:21:59.800Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "Third follow-up: reviewed and retained the prior uncommitted timing receipt. Taking over the interrupted claim. Split Node 26 quick coverage into raw-hit shards with exact merged enforcement; keep local release:check and ci-deep intact. Also repair revert-runner support copying and sampled-operation summary counts. CI timing is measured only on hosted jobs; observation ends within 30 minutes of the last push."
  - created_at: "2026-11-16T04:27:25.742Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "Implementation: Node 26 coverage has four file shards, two instrumentation workers each, original V8 function/block hit artifacts, then Node-native raw-report replay plus the existing source-presence and statement checks. Fixture proves identical LCOV and statement totals to unsharded execution, including disjoint branch/function coverage, relocated checkout URLs, and failure on a missing shard. Required test (26) is always() and fails closed over shard matrix, merge and parallel release checks. Quick jobs have a 22-minute cap, target <=15 minutes; four shards project approximately eight minutes from the previous >29-minute test lower bound, subject to file imbalance. Local release:check and CI Deep unchanged. Docs/tracker path uses pack inspection without lifecycle scripts and lightweight workflow/identity/changelog/health contracts so it does not compile; full packed/documentation input suites remain in code/deep runs. Thread PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs63vkcK: copy test/support and assert the disposable test imports; PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs63vkcO: bind operation/sequence summaries to actual sampled loop limits. No thread interaction. Source/test typechecks, lint, duplicates, docstring, identity and changelog checks passed; workflow/coverage/release contracts passed 103/103 before the final CLI-mode coverage probes. Touched integration tests are running through pm test."
  - created_at: "2026-11-16T04:29:08.669Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "Final focused harness passed through pm test: 104/104, zero failures/skips. Instrumenting coverage-gate.ts alone measured 855/855 lines, 176/176 branches and 20/20 functions before the final diagnostic-LCOV copy addition; the fixture also matches statement totals exactly. Raw-hit artifacts include shard LCOV for explicit line/branch/function diagnostics; merge uses original V8 reports rather than shard percentages. Strict tracker health passed with only pre-existing advisory findings. Previous run 43800153216 exact jobs API execution times: quick-shard (22, 1) 904 s success; quick-shard (22, 2) 657 s success; test (22) 10 s success; test (26) 1815 s cancelled. Current touched integration suites remain running; no package-wide coverage claim yet."
